WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.020
One Piece is THE BEST LIVE ACTION ADAPTATION EVER.

00:00:04.020 --> 00:00:09.600
But there are a TON OF CHANGES that were made from&nbsp;
the original story, like how instead of meeting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:15.360
Zoro tied up at the marine base he is literally&nbsp;
introduced by chopping this dude in half,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:22.380
stuffing him into a bag, and taking him straight&nbsp;
into a bar. Seriously, what is going on!?

00:00:22.380 --> 00:00:28.560
And speaking of bars, they also added NEON&nbsp;
LIGHTS to many of the bars. Like, what???&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:35.280
I guess the whole world has upgraded&nbsp;
because electricity is just a common&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:41.640
thing pretty much everywhere. It even shows&nbsp;
up on battleships and in Kaya’s mansion.

00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:47.700
But now let’s go back to the very beginning for&nbsp;
THE BIGGEST CHANGE in the entire live action.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.700 --> 00:00:53.340
That’s because Vice-Admiral Garp shows up at&nbsp;
Roger’s execution and gives this super serious&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.340 --> 00:00:58.620
speech which is not like his character from&nbsp;
the original show AT ALL. But this was just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.620 --> 00:01:05.100
the start because Garp’s ENTIRE storyline of&nbsp;
chasing down Luffy was completely made up for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:12.360
the live action. Although he did originally train&nbsp;
Koby and Helmeppo. And while I enjoyed the added&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.360 --> 00:01:17.160
development for Koby, the extra tension of&nbsp;
the marine threat, and some MIND-BLOWINGLY&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.160 --> 00:01:22.020
HILARIOUS Helmeppo scenes that we’ll talk&nbsp;
about in just a moment, the overall vibe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.020 --> 00:01:28.380
of Garp barely resembled the loose-cannon,&nbsp;
rule-breaking Vice-admiral from the anime.

00:01:28.380 --> 00:01:31.740
And speaking of the LEGENDARY Helmeppo,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.740 --> 00:01:37.260
he was pretty much just a goofy character&nbsp;
from the anime but he had the MOST SHOCKING&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.260 --> 00:01:44.580
scene in the entire live action when he was&nbsp;
caught BUTT NAKED playing with Zoro’s sword.

00:01:46.860 --> 00:01:52.200
What’s even more impressive though is the&nbsp;
ABSOLUTE POWERHOUSE of a battleship that Garp&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.200 --> 00:02:00.000
now rides around on. Honestly, this is much more&nbsp;
intimidating than his original ship in the anime.

00:02:02.160 --> 00:02:07.380
However, one of the MOST DISAPPOINTING&nbsp;
CHANGES for me was that the Live Action&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.980 --> 00:02:12.720
COMPLETELY SKIPPED the very end of&nbsp;
Luffy’s backstory. In the anime,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.720 --> 00:02:17.640
this scene shows Luffy at age 17&nbsp;
ready to set out on his adventure.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.640 --> 00:02:22.620
And as he leaves he lands a MASSIVE PUNCH that&nbsp;
completely knocks out this giant sea monster,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.620 --> 00:02:29.100
showing us all just how much Luffy has grown.&nbsp;
But nope, just completely cut from this version.

00:02:29.100 --> 00:02:33.960
But maybe they skipped it for this INSANE&nbsp;
REASON because there is no doubt in my mind&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.960 --> 00:02:39.660
that the Live Action versions of the&nbsp;
characters are WAY WEAKER than in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.660 --> 00:02:45.960
original story. I mean they were literally&nbsp;
trapped by Buggy inside a simple wooden box&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.960 --> 00:02:50.820
but Zoro and Luffy were SO WEAK that&nbsp;
they couldn’t even break out. Though&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.820 --> 00:02:56.580
later on Luffy can apparently punch through&nbsp;
stone, so a bit of a head scratcher there.

00:02:57.420 --> 00:03:02.220
One other awesome change is that Nami’s&nbsp;
first staff can now collapse into a size&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.220 --> 00:03:06.660
that can be easily carried on her&nbsp;
waist. Pretty cool if you ask me.

00:03:06.660 --> 00:03:14.100
And speaking of Nami, we see her ACTUALLY&nbsp;
DOING burglar stuff in the Live Action&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.100 --> 00:03:19.800
like breaking into a safe! Which sadly we&nbsp;
never actually saw much during the anime.

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:26.520
Plus I was COMPLETELY SHOCKED when Nami&nbsp;
saw the DEVASTATING DAMAGE Buggy did to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.520 --> 00:03:32.040
Orange Town. Damn, this had WAY&nbsp;
MORE impact than in the manga.

00:03:32.580 --> 00:03:36.000
But that’s not the only change in&nbsp;
Buggy’s part of the story because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:42.000
in the Live Action clown is 10 TIMES&nbsp;
MORE EVIL than in the anime. Originally&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:46.860
he never kidnapped all the villagers&nbsp;
or threatened to torture a little kid.

00:03:46.860 --> 00:03:51.696
And the Live Action even gave us a&nbsp;
super rare Big Brain Luffy moment,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.696 --> 00:03:57.840
when he came up with the plan to trap Buggy’s&nbsp;
body parts in the crates. If you compare this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.840 --> 00:04:03.180
exact moment to the manga it was Nami who&nbsp;
decided to tie up Buggy’s limbs with some rope.

00:04:03.180 --> 00:04:08.580
However, the reward for saving this village was&nbsp;
NOTHING COMPARED to what it was in the anime.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:08.580 --> 00:04:14.100
That’s because the Mayor of Orange Town offered&nbsp;
Live Action Luffy this tiny basket of food,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.100 --> 00:04:19.980
but in the original, the crew came away&nbsp;
with giant sacks stuffed full of goodies.

00:04:19.980 --> 00:04:25.860
This brings us to one of the MOST&nbsp;
CONTROVERSIAL changes in the Live Action,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:25.860 --> 00:04:31.140
which was all the times Nami hinted that&nbsp;
she was never going to betray the crew.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.140 --> 00:04:36.960
And while they did this weird “she’s staying,&nbsp;
oh wait she’s not staying” thing during Baratie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.960 --> 00:04:41.820
overall I feel that they kinda&nbsp;
spoiled the one mind-blowing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:41.820 --> 00:04:46.080
twist from the original East Blue story&nbsp;
when Nami abandoned the crew at Baratie.

00:04:48.840 --> 00:04:53.640
Though it was AMAZING to see these&nbsp;
mini earbud transponder snails,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:53.640 --> 00:04:56.280
which never showed up in the original story.

00:04:56.280 --> 00:05:04.260
And now we come to the SINGLE-MOST CHANGED ARC&nbsp;
of the entire story. And that is Syrup Village,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:04.260 --> 00:05:11.880
where we meet Usopp for the first time. And&nbsp;
man this place is SO DIFFERENT. Because the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:11.880 --> 00:05:19.080
Live Action turned this tiny little village in&nbsp;
the hills into a super busy shipbuilding island.

00:05:19.080 --> 00:05:25.020
And at first I HATED THIS but I&nbsp;
finally came around to like it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:25.020 --> 00:05:28.860
when the live action added Luffy&nbsp;
describing his perfect ship which&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:28.860 --> 00:05:33.240
just goes to show how important&nbsp;
the ship is as part of the crew.

00:05:33.240 --> 00:05:37.020
Plus they actually gave Usopp a&nbsp;
brand new job working on ships,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:37.020 --> 00:05:42.060
which helps explain his ability to fix up&nbsp;
the Merry during their future adventures.

00:05:43.380 --> 00:05:48.780
But that’s just the start of the WILD CHANGES&nbsp;
in Syrup Village because Nami bonding with Kaya&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:48.780 --> 00:05:53.940
was NEVER part of the original story. Though&nbsp;
I will admit the added character development&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:53.940 --> 00:06:01.440
for Kaya was awesome, and she even gave my man&nbsp;
Usopp THE VERY FIRST KISS in the entire story.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:02.100 --> 00:06:04.500
Just don’t tell Sanji about that.

00:06:04.500 --> 00:06:11.280
But then they dropped the ball on Kaya’s entire&nbsp;
story arc by cutting out THE ONE SCENE where she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:11.280 --> 00:06:20.040
actually stands up to Kuro. Seriously this was her&nbsp;
one moment to show some courage, but nope. Gone.

00:06:20.040 --> 00:06:25.740
And speaking of Kuro, they cut out almost&nbsp;
his entire crew. Which you know is kinda&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:25.740 --> 00:06:30.840
important for a pirate captain. And if that&nbsp;
wasn’t bad enough they left him with probably&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:30.840 --> 00:06:37.080
the most cringe characters in the entire show,&nbsp;
Sham and Buchi. Plus they cut out this dude,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:37.080 --> 00:06:41.400
who was one of my favorite parts&nbsp;
of this entire arc in the anime.

00:06:43.020 --> 00:06:48.180
We also have to mention the changes to this&nbsp;
sheep-head dude’s story. Unlike in the anime,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:48.180 --> 00:06:54.420
Merry is not a butler but instead he is Kaya’s&nbsp;
financial advisor. Which is honestly a bit sad&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:54.420 --> 00:07:01.140
because he was one of Kaya’s only friends in&nbsp;
her entire house. Then of course he ends up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:01.140 --> 00:07:08.160
actually dying unlike in the anime where he&nbsp;
survived and gave the crew the ship himself.

00:07:08.160 --> 00:07:12.360
But now we have some of the&nbsp;
WORST CHANGES in the live action,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:12.360 --> 00:07:17.760
which unfortunately all involve Usopp.&nbsp;
First, they took away his long nose.

00:07:21.420 --> 00:07:25.860
Then they made Usopp do LITERALLY&nbsp;
NOTHING during the final fight to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:25.860 --> 00:07:32.220
save Kaya. He is supposed to be a coward&nbsp;
who overcomes his fear, not JUST A COWARD.

00:07:32.220 --> 00:07:37.428
But the WORST PART is that he&nbsp;
cannot even fire a cannon. This&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:37.428 --> 00:07:41.880
is unacceptable! He is supposed&nbsp;
to be an expert sharpshooter who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:41.880 --> 00:07:49.320
can hit a rock super far away. That is&nbsp;
his one thing! And they took it away!

00:07:50.400 --> 00:07:53.700
But enough of Usopp, let’s talk&nbsp;
about a really dumb change for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:53.700 --> 00:07:58.620
Zoro’s backstory. That’s because in the&nbsp;
original story, we see Zoro talking to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:58.620 --> 00:08:03.360
the master of the dojo before Kuina ever&nbsp;
even dies. However, in the Live Action,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:03.360 --> 00:08:09.900
they literally never interact until Kuina’s death&nbsp;
which makes for this awkward exchange where Zoro&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:09.900 --> 00:08:13.860
has to ask for Kuina’s sword instead of&nbsp;
Koushirou giving it to him on his own.

00:08:15.360 --> 00:08:20.400
They also made Kuina’s hair super blue for&nbsp;
some weird reason, instead of its normal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:20.400 --> 00:08:26.880
black.And Zoro’s famous sword is also slightly&nbsp;
changed, as the blade is missing the normal black&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:26.880 --> 00:08:33.240
part of the blade on the non-cutting side.&nbsp;
Instead it is just this uniform shiny metal.

00:08:34.200 --> 00:08:38.160
But the change I’ve been complaining about since&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:38.160 --> 00:08:44.220
the very first promotional image is the&nbsp;
way the Merry’s figurehead looks. Uhh,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:44.220 --> 00:08:52.620
is supposed to be the perfect friendly&nbsp;
little sheep, not the stuff of nightmares.

00:08:52.620 --> 00:08:58.200
But another thing that made NO SENSE was&nbsp;
how Luffy didn’t even know that he could&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:58.200 --> 00:09:03.060
blow himself up to block this cannonball. I&nbsp;
mean he’s had his devil fruit for over ten&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:03.060 --> 00:09:08.940
years, and in the anime he was doing way&nbsp;
crazier stuff than this with no problem.

00:09:14.640 --> 00:09:20.280
Now let’s move onto probably THE MOST&nbsp;
AMAZING change in the entire live action,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:20.280 --> 00:09:28.260
which is that they turned Sanji’s pervertedness&nbsp;
meter all the way down to zero. Seriously,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:28.260 --> 00:09:32.820
it’s like he’s a new man who just happens&nbsp;
to enjoy filtering with the ladies like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:32.820 --> 00:09:38.760
Nami and Nojiko instead of being super over&nbsp;
the top weird with girls like in the anime.

00:09:38.760 --> 00:09:46.800
And honestly, almost all of the changes at&nbsp;
Bartie were FANTASTIC. It looks INCREDIBLE.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:46.800 --> 00:09:53.700
And the best part was that this place gave us&nbsp;
drunk Usopp. What else could we possibly ask for?

00:09:54.660 --> 00:09:58.440
They also changed the reason Luffy was&nbsp;
forced to work for Zeff. Originally,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:58.440 --> 00:10:01.740
Luffy launched a cannonball which&nbsp;
crashed into the floating restaurant,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:02.340 --> 00:10:06.900
so he was forced to work to pay off the damage.&nbsp;
But in the Live Action he just didn’t have any&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:06.900 --> 00:10:14.220
money to pay the bill. Which makes sense,&nbsp;
but is less cool in my humble opinion.

00:10:14.220 --> 00:10:20.820
Plus the decision to COMPLETELY ELIMINATE Don&nbsp;
Krieg from ever showing up to Baratie was a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:20.820 --> 00:10:25.740
simply amazing choice. Because while I don’t&nbsp;
love the fact that Garp felt he needed to call&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:25.740 --> 00:10:30.000
Mihawk for help, the world’s strongest&nbsp;
swordsman’s new introduction showed us&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:36.360
just how badass he truly is without wasting&nbsp;
a ton of time by bringing Kreig to Baratie.

00:10:36.360 --> 00:10:42.420
And can I just say I LOVE that they&nbsp;
introduced the fishmen in this arc. From&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:42.420 --> 00:10:47.580
this fishman serving as the restaurant's front&nbsp;
of house to Arlong showing up like a mob boss&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:47.580 --> 00:10:53.460
for the entire East Blue it all worked&nbsp;
well to expand the scope of the world.

00:10:55.260 --> 00:11:01.680
However, Arlong’s fight with Luffy in episode&nbsp;
six shows off one of the WORST MISTAKES in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:02.340 --> 00:11:05.460
the entire show. That’s because&nbsp;
when Arlong sends Luffy flying,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:05.460 --> 00:11:10.380
we can clearly see that he is actually&nbsp;
hurting from these blows. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:10.380 --> 00:11:15.840
in reality Luffy’s rubber body should make&nbsp;
him immune to damage from regular punches,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:15.840 --> 00:11:20.640
kicks, and even bullets, like we saw early&nbsp;
in episode one when Alivda smashed him with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:20.640 --> 00:11:26.220
her club and shot him. The only thing that&nbsp;
should really cause him any damage at this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:26.220 --> 00:11:31.440
point are sharp objects like blades or teeth&nbsp;
and of course the obvious threat of drowning.

00:11:31.440 --> 00:11:37.380
And the original luffy would NEVER&nbsp;
get crushed by Arlong in this scene,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:37.380 --> 00:11:41.640
because he is way stronger than the&nbsp;
fishman, but I guess we can say it’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:41.640 --> 00:11:46.080
because this version of Luffy is&nbsp;
weaker than the anime version.

00:11:46.080 --> 00:11:49.680
Also can we just point out how&nbsp;
much Usopp’s slingshot looks&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:49.680 --> 00:11:54.000
like a toy. I honestly never got that&nbsp;
feeling when seeing it in the anime.

00:11:56.280 --> 00:12:02.340
Now if you’ve watched through the Water 7 arc in&nbsp;
the anime then you should find this next new scene&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:03.600 --> 00:12:09.360
HILARIOUS! That’s because when Sanji is talking&nbsp;
to Luffy and Usopp on the Merry, he says that a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:09.360 --> 00:12:13.980
captain’s decisions are what separates him from&nbsp;
the rest of the crew. And then Luffy literally&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:13.980 --> 00:12:20.580
looks right at Usopp! Which is such a fun easter&nbsp;
egg for viewers who know what happens later on.

00:12:22.560 --> 00:12:28.020
And earlier I said Syrup village looked way&nbsp;
different, but this next set is also WAY DIFFERENT&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:28.020 --> 00:12:34.920
from its original. In the anime, Coco Village is&nbsp;
shown as a tropical paradise which hides the dark&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:34.920 --> 00:12:40.740
secrets, but in the live action they transformed&nbsp;
it into a SUPER rural village full of huts. Which&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:40.740 --> 00:12:45.600
makes sense since these people are being bed dry,&nbsp;
but I still miss the appearance of the anime.

00:12:46.320 --> 00:12:52.380
Arlong park also had a SERIOUS MAKEOVER.&nbsp;
They basically made it a club with some&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:52.380 --> 00:12:56.760
random carnival games thrown in there which&nbsp;
is a lot different from the original location.

00:12:57.480 --> 00:13:02.940
The Live Action also made a really confusing&nbsp;
choice during this arc. That’s because originally&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:02.940 --> 00:13:07.980
the people in Coco Village knew about Nami’s&nbsp;
sacrifice to work for Arlong from the very&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:07.980 --> 00:13:13.680
beginning. Which made them never hate her. But&nbsp;
in the live action, they don’t know anything&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:13.680 --> 00:13:19.020
and there’s this super rough dynamic of Nami&nbsp;
literally forcing the villagers to cough up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:19.020 --> 00:13:27.180
more cash. And these people who are supposed&nbsp;
to love her think she is a traitor. Plus then&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:27.180 --> 00:13:32.220
she had to spell it out for Nojiko so her&nbsp;
own sister wouldn’t hit her with a shovel.

00:13:33.540 --> 00:13:40.200
They also cut these two bounty hunter brothers and&nbsp;
this Octopus fishman. Which is understandable why&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:40.200 --> 00:13:46.560
they cut the octopus because honestly it would&nbsp;
take a lot of cgi to make his character work.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:46.560 --> 00:13:51.480
But he does play a pretty important role in the&nbsp;
future, so I wonder if they’ll bring him back.

00:13:52.020 --> 00:13:58.260
But now let’s discuss some awesome and also&nbsp;
bizarre changes about the world’s greatest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:58.260 --> 00:14:03.540
swordsman. In the live action Mihawk actually&nbsp;
never came to Baratie looking for Luffy. He&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:03.540 --> 00:14:08.580
only came to the floating restaurant chasing&nbsp;
after Don Kreig, but in this version he weirdly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:08.580 --> 00:14:13.620
follows actual orders from the marines&nbsp;
which is way out of character for him.

00:14:13.620 --> 00:14:18.000
The Live Action Mihawk also makes a direct&nbsp;
comment about Luffy’s hat, which is such&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:18.000 --> 00:14:23.280
cool foreshadowing of his connection to Shank.&nbsp;
And he even goes on to compare Luffy to Roger,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:23.280 --> 00:14:27.660
which is the same thing that Zeff does&nbsp;
when talking to Garp. So there a lot&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:27.660 --> 00:14:32.160
more obvious connections to Luffy and&nbsp;
Roger than WE EVER HAD in the anime.

00:14:32.160 --> 00:14:39.900
But the ABSOLUTE WORST CHANGE they made&nbsp;
to this awesome character is his boots!&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:40.440 --> 00:14:44.160
Just look at these things. And I&nbsp;
have nothing against cowboy boots,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:44.160 --> 00:14:49.260
but honestly it looks like he is ready&nbsp;
to ride a bull not fight legendary duels.

00:14:49.260 --> 00:14:57.060
And speaking of character designs, they made SO&nbsp;
MANY AMAZING improvements on characters’ outfits.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:57.060 --> 00:15:02.400
In particular the straw hats, who wear many of the&nbsp;
outfits we see on the volume covers on the manga,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:02.400 --> 00:15:05.340
instead of sticking with the same&nbsp;
clothes for most of the East Blue.

00:15:05.340 --> 00:15:11.220
Although some changes were a bit too far out&nbsp;
there for me, like Sanji literally wearing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:11.220 --> 00:15:16.140
vans while stranded during his flashback.&nbsp;
There were also Ben Beckman AND Bellemere,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:16.140 --> 00:15:20.040
who both looked much older than&nbsp;
they did in the original story.

00:15:20.040 --> 00:15:28.620
But THE WORST character design change just has to&nbsp;
be Arlong, and that’s because the dude is JUST.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:28.620 --> 00:15:36.540
TOO. SMALL. In the anime the fishman towers over&nbsp;
Luffy and the crew, which really adds a sense of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:36.540 --> 00:15:43.440
intimidation and fear. I mean just look at&nbsp;
this guy. He is basically twice as tall as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:43.440 --> 00:15:48.600
Genzo. But in the live action, he is just slightly&nbsp;
taller, which just doesn’t have the same effect.

00:15:52.560 --> 00:15:57.240
Another very odd change was that they made&nbsp;
Nami bury her treasure right next to her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:57.240 --> 00:16:05.820
mother’s grave. I mean, Nojiko even pointed&nbsp;
out how messed up that is. In the anime&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:05.820 --> 00:16:11.520
Bellemere’s grave was by the ocean and Nami&nbsp;
kept her money buried in the tangerine grove.

00:16:11.520 --> 00:16:16.140
But there is one other MAJOR change to&nbsp;
this arc that I haven’t mentioned yet,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:16.140 --> 00:16:19.920
and that is everything involving Buggy&nbsp;
the Clown, so if you want to hear my&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:19.920 --> 00:16:29.880
full thoughts on his added involvement in the&nbsp;
story you can watch my full review right here.

00:16:29.880 --> 00:16:33.480
Shanks for watching and I’ll&nbsp;
see you in the next one.

